--- !u!114 &1663125589
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1663125586}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: ce2f88b84d040c440b50f52c254e2159, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  bookName: How To Fight - Wellness
  pages:
  - In a battle, your wellness is indicated by three stats. Health, represented as
    a heart, Power, represented as a flame, & Corruption, represented by a purple
    heart.
  - The closer to death you are, the faster your heart beats, and the more damaged
    the indicator will become. If the indicator shatters, you will die.
  - Power is expended when casting spells or performing actions outside your normal
    capabilities. The more power you have accumulated, the brighter your flame will
    burn. Power can be gained by defending or using special items.
  - Corruption can be gained in many ways, mainly from interacting with unstable
